      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get the diligence part, but it's just so frustrating. it feels like these little bits of info are almost malicious, like they're intentionally popping up to mess with us right when we think we're safe. it's like having these tiny, invisible little pests living in the code that just want to cause chaos. is there any legal way to account for that kind of 'unpredictable mischief' in a compliance framework, or are we just expected to hunt them down forever?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
